dexter's names and returns kits' names: \code{visit_id} (one child at one visit), \code{pattern_id} and
\code{raw} (and \code{subj_id} for the child). Only the original output, \code{kits_original(s)} (dexter's own
table), keeps dexter's names.

Until kitsPreview 0.22.0 the columns were \code{person_id}, \code{pid}, \code{booklet_id}, \code{booklet_score}
and \code{booklet_max}. Data and \code{persons} need the new names \code{visit_id} and \code{subj_id}.
